1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,610
When I finished twelfth grade,
I was assigned to Bahir Dar University;

2
00:00:04,610 --> 00:00:06,783
right then a new chapter began.

3
00:00:07,483 --> 00:00:10,213
My journey began in Ankober;

4
00:00:10,213 --> 00:00:14,783
with only one backpack and
a mind full of questions.

5
00:00:15,483 --> 00:00:21,783
First to Debre Birhan, then to Addis
Ababa, and finally to Bahir Dar.

6
00:00:22,483 --> 00:00:27,373
As I looked out of the window, the
road and the landscape kept changing;

7
00:00:27,373 --> 00:00:31,033
forest and mountains, valleys
and roads stretching away.

8
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:34,773
It was dusk when I reached Autobus Tera;

9
00:00:34,773 --> 00:00:37,033
my friend met me there.

10
00:00:37,733 --> 00:00:45,158
People move every way, cars pass,
and brokers ask, "Do you want a bed?"

11
00:00:45,858 --> 00:00:51,158
For a moment everything seemed
too much at once, and confusing.

12
00:00:51,858 --> 00:00:55,508
In the end we chose a room with one bed;

13
00:00:55,508 --> 00:01:00,575
it was not the best, and not bad,
but clean enough to rest.

14
00:01:01,275 --> 00:01:03,929
Next morning, to continue the journey,

15
00:01:03,929 --> 00:01:07,117
we stood in a long queue
and bought a ticket.

16
00:01:07,817 --> 00:01:11,126
When I remember that first
night away from home,

17
00:01:11,126 --> 00:01:16,397
I say one thing to all who leave the
familiar world and start a new journey:

18
00:01:16,397 --> 00:01:18,987
the first night is always confusing.

19
00:01:18,987 --> 00:01:22,617
Do not run. Savour it.

